p>The Gemma 4 architecture is in many ways like the Gemma 3 series of model=
s, with some changes here and there. There are a number of things that were=
 changed compared to Gemma 3 that relate to all model sizes:</p><ul><li><p>=
<strong>Interleaving Layers </strong><span>=E2=80=93 Global attention is al=
ways the last layer</span></p></li><li><p><strong>K=3DV </strong><span>=E2=
=80=93 The Keys are set to be equivalent to the Values only for the global =
attention</span></p></li><li><p><strong>p-RoPE </strong><span>=E2=80=93 Low=
-frequency-pruned RoPE applied to the embeddings</span></p></li></ul><p>Som=
e of the models are a bit different than others (e.g., only small models us=
e Per-Layer Embeddings). Before we go into the specifics of each model, let=
=E2=80=99s explore in more detail what they have in common.</p><h2 class=3D=
"header-anchor-post">Interleaving Layers<div class=3D"pencraft pc-display-f=
lex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-parent=
"><div class=3D"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA"><div=
