button></div></div></h3><p>An important component of any Large Language Mod=
el is how it keeps track of the order of words in a sequence. One of the mo=
st common techniques is called Rotary Positional Encodings (RoPE). RoPE tak=
es the Query and Key vectors and slices them up into pairs of two values. E=
ach pair can now be seen as a vector in 2-dimensional space pointing toward=
s a direction. RoPE rotates this direction slightly for each pair of values=
 at decreasing speeds. The first pair has a large rotation compared to the =
last pair. This rotation allows the model to track the relative distances b=
etween words.</p><div class=3D"captioned-image-container"><figure><a target=
