=3D"14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>High =
frequency pairs are very sensitive to small changes in position due to the =
amount of information they were given at the first place (large rotation). =
They are great for tracking a word=E2=80=99s position. The low frequency pa=
irs, however, are given a very slight rotation and barely move at all from =
word to word. Since these low frequency pairs only contain minimal position=
al information, and are closest to what the original KQ values were, they a=
re more suitable for tracking semantic content. As such, they stay the most=
 true to what they originally were (without positional information).</p><di=
